      "rationale": "Extending type-partitioned retrieval from RetypeR's single type (Python type errors) to 18 categories across 3 languages and comparing against ReinFix's soft joint embedding is incremental but well-motivated. No concurrent work found doing exactly this, but the idea is a natural next step that any practitioner familiar with RetypeR and ReinFix would identify. The EMNLP-specific NLP contribution (cross-lingual taxonomy induction consistency) is too thin to lift the novelty score—it's essentially a reliability check on an LLM classifier, not a fundamental NLP finding."
