      "rationale": "The compute budget (88–190 H100-hours) is within the 200-H100-hour constraint, and the DebugBench + SWE-bench Lite evaluation scope is appropriately scoped. However, the corpus sparsity concern is fundamental: the Java subset yields only ~31 instances per type on average, making k=5 retrieval nearly trivial (top-5 from 31 instances = top-16%). For rare categories (concurrency, resource leaks), the sub-index may have fewer than 20 instances—at which point type-conditioned retrieval degrades to a lookup table rather than semantic retrieval. The annotation pipeline and Defects4J Java-8 pre-filter are sound."
    },
