  "issues": [
    "CRITICAL — Citation error: ReinFix is confirmed ICSE 2026 (arXiv 2506.23100 states 'Accepted by ICSE 2026'), not ICSE 2025 as the proposal states throughout. EMNLP 2026 explicitly warns against hallucinated citations and has stated it may desk-reject papers with such errors. Every reference to 'ReinFix (ICSE 2025)' must be corrected to 'ReinFix (ICSE 2026)'.",
    "HIGH — Corpus sparsity renders type partitioning semantically degenerate for rare types: 559 Java pairs (Defects4J + GitBug-Java) across 18 types yields ~31 Java instances per type on average. For rare bug categories (concurrency, resource leaks, format errors), this may be 5–15 instances. Retrieving k=5 from a sub-index of 15 instances is not retrieval—it is exhaustive lookup. The proposal must either (a) restrict to the 6–8 most frequent types where >50 Java instances exist, or (b) merge rare types into a broader category, or (c) acknowledge that the per-type ablation is only meaningful for the top N types and report per-type corpus sizes in the paper.",
    "HIGH — Classifier error propagation is unaddressed: if the type classifier misclassifies an incoming bug (which will occur for edge cases and multi-type bugs), the system retrieves from the wrong partition and almost certainly underperforms soft retrieval for those instances. This is the main structural risk of hard partitioning over soft embedding. The proposal must analyze: (a) classifier accuracy on held-out annotated bugs, (b) the performance degradation attributable to misclassification, and (c) whether a confidence-gated fallback to soft retrieval recovers performance.",
